**StarBUG Coffee Shop
Your task is to create a StarBUG coffee shop billing system that includes only these two objects (aka., classes) called CupOfCoffee and CustomerBill in which compose of the following attributes:

CupOfCoffee The object of this class represents a cup of coffee.

coffee_type: string. There are 6 types of coffee: Espresso, Americano, Cappuccino, Latte, Mocha and Macchiato.
drinking_type: string. There are 3 types of coffee brewing styles: Hot, Cold and Frappe.
add_on: list of string. There are 3 types of coffee add-ons: Espresso shot, Syrup and Cream milk. No duplicate items should be added to a cup of coffee.
price: int. The price of this cup of coffee, initially with "no" add-on.
Create the given instance methods:

__init__(self, coffee_type, drinking_type, price)	Construct a CupOfCoffee object, initially with "no" add-on.
set_add_on(self, one_add_on, one_add_on_price)	Add one add-on and update the coffee price with one_add_on_price.
__repr__(self)	Return the detail string of this cup of coffee with the following format: " This cup is {self.drinking_type.lower()} {self.coffee_type} with no add on, {self.price} baht."
or " This cup is {self.drinking_type.lower()} {self.coffee_type} with {self.add_on[0]}, {self.price} baht."
or " This cup is {self.drinking_type.lower()} {self.coffee_type} with {", ".join(self.add_on[:-1])} and {self.add_on[-1]}, {self.price} baht."
Example. " This cup is hot Macchiato with Espresso shot and Cream milk, 180 baht."
CustomerBill The object of this class represents one customer's (ordered coffee) bill.

name: string. The customer's name.
ordered_coffee: list of CupOfCoffee objects, i.e., the coffee order sequence.
Create the given instance methods:

__init__(self, name)	Construct a CustomerBill object, initially with "no" ordered coffee.
add_ordered_coffee(self, aCupOfCoffeeObject)	Add a CupOfCoffee object into thr ordered_coffee list.
receipt(self)	Return the string of a receipt with details of all customer's ordered cups of coffee. See the test case and the sample output and format.
Flow Control Hint

The starBUG coffee billing system starts with asking the coffee menu (CoffeeMenu01/02.txt) and add-on menu (CoffeeMenuAddOn01/02.txt) available here (ที่นี่) of that operation day.
 Note: Any product type with a price of 0 baht means that the product is not available for sale.

Then it will ask for the customer's name, number of cups of coffee to order, type of coffee, drinking type, and add-on following the given menu.

For each customer, your task is to create a CustomerBill object with CupOfCoffee object(s) and the billing system itself will operates the cafe.

Until the customer name is Good Day, the system will print a report that concludes the number of coffees sold that day and then stop.

Sample output can be found (ที่นี่).

See the test case and the sample output and format for more detail.

